---
// Dojo Tutor case study.
import CaseStudy from '../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Stats from '../components/Stats.astro';
import HeroWall from '../components/HeroWall.astro';
import Pic from '../components/Pic.astro';
import { recent } from '../data/site';

// Link to the pricing deep dive once it's published (always in local preview).
const pricing = recent.find((r) => r.href === '/tutor-pricing');
const showPricing = pricing && (!pricing.draft || import.meta.env.DEV);
---

<CaseStudy
  name="Dojo Tutor"
  tagline="ClassDojo: Designing and building the marketplace tools Dojo Tutor was missing."
  details={[
    { label: 'Responsibilities', items: ['Product design', 'User research', 'Product building'] },
    { label: 'Collaborators', items: ['1 product manager', '4 engineers'] },
    { label: 'Platforms', items: ['Web', 'iOS and Android (launching Dec 2026)'] },
    { label: 'Years', items: ['2024–Present'] },
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="headline">
    ClassDojo: Designing and building the marketplace tools <strong>Dojo Tutor</strong> was missing.
  </Fragment>

  <Stats
    slot="meta"
    items={[
      { value: '70%+', label: 'of surfaces designed' },
      { value: '50%+', label: 'of the frontend built with AI coding agents' },
      { value: '+20%', label: 'Lifetime value, year over year' },
      { value: '+12%', label: '3-month retention (relative)' },
    ]}
  />

  <div class="intro">
    <p>
      Dojo Tutor is ClassDojo’s marketplace connecting tutors and families across a wide range of subjects, in both
      1-on-1 and group formats. I design for everyone it serves: tutors running their businesses, parents managing
      their children’s learning, students in class, and the internal team that manages the platform behind the
      scenes. I own the core experience end to end, from research and early concepts through high-fidelity design and
      implementation, often shipping features myself with AI coding agents.
    </p>
  </div>

  <figure class="figure wide">
    <HeroWall
      alt="A wall of Dojo Tutor screens across web and mobile: calendars, chats, pricing, group classes, insights, and the parent home"
      eager
    />
  </figure>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>From matching service to marketplace: +20% LTV year over year</h2>
    <p>
      Dojo Tutor launched in 2023 as a matching service, and demand quickly outpaced what the MVP was built for.
      Engineering was rightly focused on growth and on paying down the tech debt from sprinting to launch, which left the
      core tools a marketplace needs, like schedule management, messaging, and pricing, sitting in the backlog.
    </p>
    <p>
      Since joining in 2024, I’ve redesigned every post-purchase surface for tutors and families. I’ve also added the
      core features a marketplace needs: schedule management, tutor-set pricing, direct messaging, automated marketing
      tools, and payment management.
    </p>
    <p>These additions have enabled tutors to better retain families thereby increasing LTV by +20% YoY.</p>
  </div>

  <Figure
    images={[
      { name: 'dojo-calendar-week', alt: 'Tutor week calendar' },
      { name: 'dojo-chats', alt: 'Direct messaging between a tutor and parents' },
    ]}
    tight
  />
  <Figure
    images={[
      { name: 'dojo-subscriptions', alt: 'Tutor subscriptions list' },
      { name: 'dojo-notifications', alt: 'Tutor notification settings' },
    ]}
    lead="Core marketplace tools."
  >
    Schedule management, direct messaging, subscriptions, and notification settings for tutors.
  </Figure>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Engineers were backed up so I learned to build product myself</h2>
    <p>
      I taught myself to ship production frontend with AI coding agents like Codex and Claude Code and am now releasing
      to production every week.
    </p>
    <p>
      AI agents make it easy to produce a lot of UI quickly. The challenge is keeping it coherent and well crafted. I
      set up Dojo Tutor’s design system so AI-generated UI stays on-pattern, and I review and refine what agents
      produce before it ships.
    </p>
    <p>
      Since then I’ve built over half of Dojo Tutor’s frontend surfaces across the parent- and tutor-facing experiences,
      with backend contributions as well, all without pulling engineers off growth work. This includes updated calendar
      and performance metrics tools for tutors, and a new homepage for parents to manage their classes and find new
      tutors and group classes.
    </p>
    <p>
      My workflow included setting up Dojo Tutor’s design system to integrate smoothly with AI-generated UI and partnering
      with engineers during the planning process before implementing and responding to both manual and automated code
      reviews.
    </p>
    <p>
      My AI-powered workflows are constantly being refined with new models, AI-native design tools, and test suites for
      code quality.
    </p>
  </div>

  <figure class="figure video">
    <video
      class="wide"
      src="/media/dojo-design-system-components.mp4"
      poster="/media/dojo-design-system-components-poster.jpg"
      width="1920"
      height="1080"
      autoplay
      muted
      loop
      playsinline
      preload="metadata"
      aria-label="Dojo Tutor design system components: navigation, notification settings, calendars, earnings, subscriptions, pricing, and class management"
    ></video>
    <figcaption>
      <strong>Patterns that keep the product coherent as it grows.</strong>{' '}<span class="muted"
        >The design system covers everything from page layouts to individual components, along with how user lockups,
        date and time ranges, and other bits are displayed.</span
      >
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Using AI to make tutors more effective</h2>
    <p>
      We use AI transcription to turn class recordings into automated recaps and progress reports for families. I
      designed the flows that allow tutors to review and edit anything AI-generated before it’s sent, so they stay in
      control of what goes out in their name.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also designed Tutor Clips, where AI finds the most compelling moments in a session and sends families a short
      clip, so everyone stays in the loop between classes.
    </p>
    <p>
      Finally I designed an in-class AI assistant that pulls up context from previous lessons and offers suggestions,
      especially when a tutor is trying to turn a trial class into a subscription.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Group classes: +10% revenue, with safety review built in</h2>
    <p>
      Dojo Tutor launched with 1-on-1 online tutoring only. In early 2026, we introduced group classes, our largest
      product expansion to date.
    </p>
    <p>
      I designed the tutor experience for creating and managing group classes, along with the internal tools our team
      uses to review class submissions for inappropriate or unsafe content, class quality, and to provide feedback that
      will help tutors with converting students.
    </p>
    <p>Within the first 8 months of launch, group classes grew Dojo Tutor’s overall revenue by 10%.</p>
  </div>

  <Figure
    images={[
      { name: 'dojo-group-classes', alt: 'Group classes dashboard' },
      { name: 'dojo-group-class-detail', alt: 'Group class detail with sections and enrollment' },
    ]}
    lead="Group class management."
  >
    Tutors list classes, then open sections and track enrollment across them.
  </Figure>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Tutor-set pricing: 70% of tutors opted in within 3 months</h2>
    <p>
      Prices used to be fixed by the platform. Dojo Tutor sought to allow tutors to set their own prices, allowing them to
      charge more for specialty topics as well as open up more affordable tutoring options for families.
    </p>
    <p>
      Research showed that while the majority of tutors were interested in setting their own prices, many were concerned
      about a “race to the bottom” as tutors competed on price. This informed how we calculated marketplace fees to
      increase tutor take-home pay as well as working with tutors to communicate their value instead of treating their
      tutoring as an undifferentiated experience in the marketplace.
    </p>
    <p>
      I designed and built much of the frontend for tutor pricing, including the first-time experience, setting rates,
      adding discounts, and surfacing market data so tutors can price competitively.
    </p>
    <p>
      Despite widespread apprehension from our tutor community, over 70% of tutors opted into the new pricing model within
      the first 3 months of release.
    </p>
    {
      showPricing && (
        <p>
          <a class="more" href="/tutor-pricing">Read the full pricing case study ›</a>
        </p>
      )
    }
  </div>

  <figure class="figure pair tight">
    <div class="grid" style="--cols: 2">
      <Pic
        name="dojo-pricing-details"
        alt="Pricing details before confirming: payout rates, Earnings Boost, trial pay, and the tutor's new class prices and discounts"
        sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 585px"
      />
      <video
        src="/media/dojo-pricing-hero.mp4"
        poster="/media/dojo-pricing-hero-poster.jpg"
        width="1920"
        height="1080"
        autoplay
        muted
        loop
        playsinline
        preload="metadata"
        aria-label="Setting a group class price: recommended range, take-home pay after the platform fee, and Earnings Boost"
      ></video>
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      <strong>Pricing with guardrails.</strong>{' '}<span class="muted"
        >Market-based recommended ranges, take-home pay after fees, and the Earnings Boost for long-term family
        relationships.</span
      >
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  <Figure
    images={[
      { name: 'dojo-pricing-earnings', alt: 'Estimated earnings increase from the new pricing model' },
      { name: 'dojo-pricing-setup', alt: 'Setting 1:1 tutoring prices during onboarding' },
    ]}
    lead="Opting in."
  >
    Tutors see what they stand to earn before switching, then set prices with recommendations based on similar
    classes.
  </Figure>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Native tutor apps from zero to one, launching December 2026</h2>
    <p>
      I designed native iOS and Android apps that let tutors message families, manage their classes, and claim open
      spots in classes that need a substitute.
    </p>
    <p>
      Push notifications allow for more responsiveness when talking to prospective students as well as active
      subscribers. They also allow us to inform tutors of classes in need of a substitute similar to the dispatch model
      of rideshare apps.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure
    images={[{ name: 'dojo-app-phones', alt: 'Tutor app: classes, chat, last-minute substitution, and menu' }]}
    lead="Tutor app."
  >
    Classes, chat, claiming a last-minute substitution, and the account menu.
  </Figure>
</CaseStudy>

<style>
  /* A screenshot beside a video: the video is cropped to the screenshot's 4:3 so the
     pair sits level (its edges are empty background). */
  .pair video {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: #fdf6ee;
  }
  .video video {
    max-width: none;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: #fdf6ee;
  }
</style>
